WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.050 line:15%
Famously Greenland was settled by the Vikings

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.649 line:15%
and I just ran into the first guy here

3
00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:08.270
who looks like a Viking, Nicky.

4
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.470
You look like a Viking.

5
00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.970
You also look like a clean-up hitter

6
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.356
for the Boston Red Sox.

7
00:00:13.356 --> 00:00:14.189
Okay.

8
00:00:14.189 --> 00:00:15.383
Yeah.

9
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:20.058 line:15%
What?

10
00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:22.308
Oh, you can buy a gun here?

11
00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.760
But there's no gun violence here.

12
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.593
(audience laughs)

13
00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:40.360
Wait, you walked for three days?

14
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.193
Yeah.

15
00:00:41.193 --> 00:00:42.026
What are you, Johnny Appleseed?

16
00:00:42.026 --> 00:00:43.970 line:15%
What are you --
(audience laughs)

17
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:44.803
Well you don't need to.

18
00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:45.890
It's a very funny reference

19
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.260
and people in my country will laugh,

20
00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.118
and people in your country won't see this.

21
00:00:49.118 --> 00:00:50.260
Yeah.

22
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.217
Here's the point,

23
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.583
you walked for three days, why?

24
00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:57.420
(audience laughs)

25
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.847
So next time you go for a walk for three days,

26
00:00:59.847 --> 00:01:02.138 line:15%
do you think you'll--

27
00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:02.971
Sure, I'll come.

28
00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:05.388 line:15%
Do we bring any food with us?

29
00:01:07.064 --> 00:01:10.731
And just eat it raw on the side of the road?

30
00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.227
Have you eaten a raw deer?

31
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.303 line:15%
You ate a raw liver of a reindeer.

32
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.460
Well, yeah, you're not an animal.

33
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.840
(audience laughs)

34
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.507
This is incredible, you are, you have true Viking blood.

35
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:36.973
Oh, you think I would pass for Viking?

36
00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:41.389
You think I seem manly enough to to be a Viking?

37
00:01:41.389 --> 00:01:42.222
(audience laughs)
Fix what?

38
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:43.210
When I'm talking about me now?

39
00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.240
Why fix something?

40
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.657
What do you mean?

41
00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:51.500
(audience laughs)

42
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.206
Soon after my arrival I was interviewed by KNR,

43
00:01:54.206 --> 00:01:58.623
Greenland's biggest and only television station.

44
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:21.603
Hi, how are you?

45
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:22.436
How are you?

46
00:02:22.436 --> 00:02:24.050
I'm good, I was just wandering in these rocks.

47
00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.660
Yeah, isn't it beautiful?

48
00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.130
Beautiful and I saw you doing a story

49
00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.463 line:15%
and I thought I'd come over.

50
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.960 line:15%
Well it felt like a really fun opportunity

51
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.970 line:15%
to come here and meet everybody,

52
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.370
and if I come here as part of my show,

53
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.178
I don't have to pay for it.

54
00:02:47.178 --> 00:02:48.011
(audience laughs)

55
00:02:48.011 --> 00:02:48.844
The show pays for it.

56
00:02:48.844 --> 00:02:50.788 line:15%
So this is a free trip for me, yeah.

57
00:02:50.788 --> 00:02:53.621 line:15%
(audience laughs)

58
00:02:59.555 --> 00:03:03.305
It's the first country to sell for that much.

59
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.340
The golf course.

60
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.780
You have a golf course.

61
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.708
It's called the Golf Klub.

62
00:03:14.708 --> 00:03:16.374 line:15%
(audience laughs)

63
00:03:16.374 --> 00:03:19.207
(audience laughs)

64
00:03:28.712 --> 00:03:30.348 line:15%
(audience laughs and cheers)

65
00:03:30.348 --> 00:03:31.181
Who do

66
00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.240
inspired the most?

67
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.330
Wow, it's hard to say.

68
00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.640
I mean, I've been inspired by so many people.

69
00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.050
The Kellogg Family.

70
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.910
I think his name is William Kellogg.

71
00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.260
You know he was the first person to make breakfast cereal.

72
00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.910
I had not a always happy childhood,

73
00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.790
and one of the things I took solace in was sugar cereals.

74
00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.420 line:15%
Your Cocoa Krispies, your Captain Crunch,

75
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.677 line:15%
your Captain Crunch with Crunch Berries,

76
00:03:54.677 --> 00:03:55.638 line:15%
(audience laughs)

77
00:03:55.638 --> 00:03:58.767 line:15%
Cocoa Puff, anything with chocolate in it,

78
00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:02.392
and Marshmallows Lucky Charms, Kellogg's did a lot of that,

79
00:04:02.392 --> 00:04:03.225
(audience laughs)

80
00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:04.560
and so they actually influenced my childhood,

81
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.740
and they're one of the reasons today

82
00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.727
that I can't lift things above my shoulder.

83
00:04:07.727 --> 00:04:08.733
(audience laughs)

84
00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:11.733
Because it's not good for you, yeah.

85
00:04:21.874 --> 00:04:24.540
The next stop on my Greenland press tour

86
00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.930
was an interview and photo shoot

87
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.980
with the CEO of Greenland's biggest and only airline.

88
00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.300 line:15%
Jacob, thank you for having me to your wonderful country.

89
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.800 line:15%
Thank you for coming here.

90
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.500
I very much enjoy your airline.

91
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.770
It has long been my dream

92
00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.550
to be in an in-flight magazine.

93
00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.383
Yeah?

94
00:04:39.383 --> 00:04:40.850
I've always wanted to be in an in-flight magazine.

95
00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.830
And I've tried and tried and tried,

96
00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.380
got very close with Virgin Atlantic once,

97
00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.248
and then they found out that I was a virgin.

98
00:04:48.248 --> 00:04:49.169
(audience laughs)

99
00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:50.460
They thought that was bad publicity.

100
00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.210
What's been your impression of Greenland

101
00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.320
and the Greenland people?

102
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.344
This is a stunning country, absolutely beautiful.

103
00:04:56.344 --> 00:04:59.130
Also, and I'm gonna go out on a limb here,

104
00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.100
but I'm gonna say that no country I've ever been to

105
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.620
has better dried fish.

106
00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.239
You guys kill it with dried fish.

107
00:05:05.239 --> 00:05:06.072
(audience laughs)

108
00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.140
I don't know what you do,

109
00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.370
but no one dries a fish like you guys.

110
00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.060
And what a great way to experience fish.

111
00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:11.893
Yeah.

112
00:05:11.893 --> 00:05:14.490
You know, you can keep the fish in your wallets.

113
00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.430
You can keep then in a fanny pack.

114
00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:16.263
(audience laughs)

115
00:05:16.263 --> 00:05:19.930
You can use the dried pressed fish as a bookmark,

116
00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.240
and then when you're done with the book,

117
00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.713
you can eat the bookmark, the fish.

118
00:05:22.713 --> 00:05:24.320
It's amazing.

119
00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.568
I see people walking around.

120
00:05:25.568 --> 00:05:28.049
They trade them like old baseball cards.

121
00:05:28.049 --> 00:05:28.882
(audience laughs)

122
00:05:28.882 --> 00:05:29.715
I don't know who's out there

123
00:05:29.715 --> 00:05:31.687
with a blow dryer on the beach,

124
00:05:31.687 --> 00:05:35.220
but I think you're just doing an amazing job.

125
00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.640
Oh, excellent, thank you, Conan.

126
00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.460
And before I knew it, I was back at KNR Studios

127
00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.020
to lend a little star power to their nightly broadcast.

128
00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.940
Please keep in mind, this really aired

129
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.690
all across Greenland.

130
00:05:54.661 --> 00:05:56.650 line:15%
Good evening, I'm Conan O'Brien,

131
00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:59.581 line:15%
and I'm bringing you the latest weather report

132
00:05:59.581 --> 00:06:00.449 line:15%
(audience cheers and claps)

133
00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:01.437 line:15%
for Greenland.

134
00:06:01.437 --> 00:06:05.320 line:15%
I will give the report in the Greenlandic language

135
00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.420
'cause let's face it, how hard could it be?

136
00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:10.253
(audience laughs)

137
00:06:19.584 --> 00:06:23.334
(audience laughs and cheers)

138
00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.774
There's cold stuff coming.

139
00:06:53.774 --> 00:06:57.441
(audience claps and cheers)

